# Shapes Reference

## Overview

A shape is a formation in absolute field coordinates, with no time (timeline spec 5.1 and 5.2): `line`, `freehand`, `circle`, `box` or `block`. A transition moves its marchers into a shape (`dest_shape_id`). Shapes live in the `timeline_shapes` table and are read through the timeline resolver.

The page-era shape system (`shape_pages`, `MarcherShape`, `EditablePath`, the canvas shape hooks) and the Fabric-drawn spec-shape handles (P7.11) no longer exist. The box shape tool is being rebuilt on the three.js field (fork #204, on hold).

## Key Files

All under `apps/desktop/`.

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `electron/database/migrations/schema.ts` (`timeline_shapes`) | The table |
| `src/timeline/timelineShapeEditor.ts` | Plans shape edits: kinds, frames, blockers, `applyShapeEdit` |
| `src/components/inspector/TimelineShapesEditor.tsx` | The inspector's shape editor (typed inputs) |
| `src/timeline/timelineErrorMessages.ts` | Refusals (E-S1, E-T3, E-T4) as toasts |

## Rules

- Write shapes only through the planned db-functions inside `transactionWithHistory`; a change that writes nothing is planned as `null` and skipped.
- Geometry is validated by the db-functions (I-S1, E-S1) before anything is written.
- New field interactions for shapes belong in `src/field/editor/` with an SVG overlay in `src/field/three/FieldOverlay.tsx` (see `docs/field/porting-fabric-features.md`).
